<title>USA: First of Michigan to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>First of Michigan to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>First of Michigan Capital Corp said Wednesday its board of directors has authorized the repurchase of up to 350,000 shares of its outstanding common stock.  </p>
<p>This authorization replaces previous board action taken in November 1995 authorizing up to 250,000 shares of which about 42,000 shares have been purchased, the company said. About 308,000 remain authorized for purchase.</p>
<p>The company had about 2.6 million shares outstanding at the end of the fiscal 1996 fourth quarter.</p>
<p>First of Michigan shares closed down 3/8 at 8-1/4 Wednesday on the Chicago Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
